# `yo fix <path> --migrate cloned-accessors` rewrites a copying accessor call
# whose result carries a unique buffer (`String`, a std collection, an
# aggregate holding one) to its `<name>_cloned` sibling from the impl registry:
# `maps.get(...)` becomes `maps.get_cloned(...)` and `maps.first()` becomes
# `maps.first_cloned()`. Since B8 the fixture's elements are `HashMap`s:
# a `String` element's copy is E0901 now, so that file no longer evaluates
# (issues/questions/2026-10-27-what-the-implicit-copy-audit-and-the-explicit-copy-migration-cover-after-b8.md,
# Option 1). YO_AUDIT_COPYING_ACCESSOR prints the same sites the
# migration records (N7): one [copying-accessor] line per call site, from the
# migration's own evaluation. The trailing `check` proves the rewritten file
# still evaluates. Plans/VALUES_BY_DEFAULT.md decision 20; lookahead §4.2 B6-b.
env=YO_AUDIT_COPYING_ACCESSOR=1
stdout_keep=^(fix:|main\.yo:[0-9]+:[0-9]+ \[copying-accessor\] )
timeout=240
